    "message": "test: keep large host processor fixtures off the stack\n\nWindows native CI reports crashes in three snapshot host-test paths after the instrument body state enlarged each processor. Move 34 named fixtures and one temporary to heap ownership, preserving their existing references, scopes, constructor arguments, destruction order and assertions.\n\nKeep the 8 MiB test stack reserve and all acceptance thresholds unchanged. Actual JUCE syntax and optimized GCC compilation pass; measured main and performance-test frames fall from 1.75 MB and 3.50 MB to 3,984 and 1,072 bytes. Native Windows execution will verify the correction.\n\nNo shipping DSP, plug-in, preset, parameter or workflow code changes.",
